## Context

First child of tracker 0801, and **it runs before any code**, on the author's
ruling of 2026-09-16: "design doc en premier, c'est lui qu'on veut reviewer
d'abord." The model is the thing he wants to read and argue with; an
implementation reviewed instead would be arguing about the model through its
consequences.

This reverses what 0801 said in an earlier revision ("not before the code"),
and the reason that rule existed is handled by *how* this ticket writes, not by
delaying it: the section is marked as a **design under review**, not as a
description of shipped behaviour. A reader must never mistake it for the
plugin's current state.

## What to write

Into `plugins/sdt-sitter/DESIGN-NOTES.md`, which has 475 lines, six sections,
the open-questions ledger, and — tellingly — **no section on the state model at
all**. The one variable that produced three defects in twelve hours is the one
thing the design document never described.

The content is settled and lives in tracker 0801; do not re-derive it:

- Two axes whose **product** is the state, not a hierarchy. Outer: `RUNNING`,
  `PAUSED`, `DEFERRED`, `ERROR`, `ENDING`, `VANISHED`. Inner: `census`,
  `draining`, `extracting`, `idle`. The proof they are orthogonal is that
  `extracting` stays true under `DEFERRED`.
- `DEFERRED` carries a **set** of reasons, not one. Today `blocked()` returns
  the first condition matched in its own evaluation order, so the displayed
  reason is arbitrary among the true ones and lifting the first manufactures a
  phantom transition.
- Each reason declares a **presentation class**: legible to the user as an
  event with a beginning and an end (a sync), or transient machine noise
  (`cpu-busy`). That field is what 0797's checkbox reads, instead of
  special-casing a phase by literal name.
- Why the product is not unfolded into twenty-four flat names.
- A **pointer** to the transition-graph artifact of 0806, never a copy of it.

Re-read open question 6 against this model rather than leaving it as written —
its partial answer was drafted before the axes were distinguished.

## Test

None; this is prose. The gate is the author's reading.

## Verification

- [ ] The section is unmistakably marked as a design under review, not as
      shipped behaviour — a reader landing on it cold cannot conclude the
      plugin works this way today
- [ ] It points at 0806's artifact rather than duplicating it
- [ ] Open question 6 re-read, and either amended or explicitly left
- [ ] `make check` green

## Invariants

- No code changes. None.
- The existing sections and the ledger keep their register.

## Exit criteria

The author has read the model as a document and either accepted it or said what
to change, before 0804 starts.
